<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST39"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Today4evr<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Today4evr<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, May 22, 2004 - 5:49 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;ve noticed a pattern to BTK&#39;s choice of victims:  <BR> <BR>First he chose the Otero&#39;s, a family. <BR>Second, Kathryn Bright or another single victim, one. <BR>Third, Shirley Vian, a family. <BR>Fourth, Nancy Fox, single victim, one. <BR>Fifth, Vickie Wegerle, a family. <BR> <BR>I&#39;m not sure if this means anything, but the pattern is there. And not having much to go on as far as how he chooses his victims, other than him stating in a letter that they are random, there is this pattern of his &#34;confessed to murders&#34;. <BR> <BR>Thinking it would take much more planning to murder a victim/victims of more than one living in a house, it may indicate something about his mental state and other matters.  <BR> <BR>Since there was no sign of forced entry at the Otero, Vian, Wegerle murder scene, I think he used the ID&#39;s to gain access to scope the situation out.  Taking immense precautions to protect himself from the known men who lived in those homes. Makes me wonder how many other family homes he tried to gain access to with an ID, that he was not allowed into for whatever reasons.  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 39-->
<!--Post: 49--><!--Time: 1085272751-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST49"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lisa<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lisa<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, May 22, 2004 - 5:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Was the lady that he waited for belonging to a family and if so, what date did he wait for her and where does she fall into all of this?  Maybe he did try and keep this pattern up that you are talking about.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 49-->
<!--Post: 50--><!--Time: 1085272973-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST50"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, May 22, 2004 - 5:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lisa, that info is available elsewhere on the site...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 50-->
<!--Post: 51--><!--Time: 1085275671-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST51"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitaboy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitaboy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, May 22, 2004 - 6:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I tend to believe BTK in the fact that they are random.  First of all those are the only known victims.  There is speculation of other victims which would throw off this theory.  Unfortunately I think when the dust settles you will find a lot more victims.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 51-->
<!--Post: 124--><!--Time: 1085789176-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST124"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sandy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sandy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 28, 2004 - 5:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe he chose his victims to fill his fantasy.But I don&#39;t believe he just went, eeny meeny miney moe,then walked up to the door. I believe he watched these people for maybe days,to see what would be the best time for him to go in and kill them.He took his time as if he knew he had plenty of it. If he knew any of the victims ,I don&#39;t believe he would admit to it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
